          "id": "review_design:5:1",
          "impact": "Implementation can satisfy fail-closed rules by returning incomplete for every run, leaving the requested portable test runner unusable without this being discovered until late.",
          "lens": "truth",
          "material": true,
          "note": null,
          "response": null,
          "rounds": 1,
          "status": "resolved",
          "target": "design",
          "target_attempt": 7,
          "target_fp": "v1:sha256:432dc9b8adab34dc5a395a74e48cfa3a84d839a1220f85d67bc858a8207395a1",
          "text": "The design promises an ordinary-Git, unprivileged committed-target execution path but does not identify a concrete viable mechanism on any supported platform that maintains immutable inputs or reliably observes every modification and loss of coverage for the whole run. A private temporary checkout or read-only file permissions alone are expressly insufficient because the test process or another same-user process can modify and revert input bytes. Define an initial supported-platform mechanism and early real-platform feasibility test demonstrating both a passing full run and invalidation on edit-and-revert/observation loss, or bring the owner a concrete tradeoff if none is feasible.",
          "upheld": false
        }
      ],
